1. Open Wireshark.
2. Select active Wi-Fi interface.
3. Double-click to start capture.
4. Open YouTube.
5. Play a video for 20–30 seconds.
6. Return to Wireshark.
7. Click Stop.

FILTERS:
dns
quic
udp
tls
tcp

8. Enter dns > Enter.
9. Observe DNS requests.
10. Enter quic > Enter.
11. Observe QUIC packets, if available.
12. Enter tls > Enter.
13. Observe encrypted traffic.
14. Select packets to view details.
15. Open Statistics > I/O Graphs.
16. Observe network traffic.

OUTPUT:
- Source IP
- Destination IP
- Protocol
- Packet length
- DNS requests
- Traffic graph
